# Xcode generated project (regenerate via: xcodegen generate)
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/

# Archives & exports
*.ipa
*.dSYM/
*.dSYM.zip

# Localization pipeline: Xcode's key set, read straight out of the build's
# `.stringsdata`. Derived from build output, not source, so it is regenerated by
# `refresh.sh` rather than committed.
#
# Committing it would be actively unsafe: `build-catalog.mjs` prunes catalog keys
# that are not in this set, so a stale copy — from a different machine, or from
# before a string was added — would delete live keys. Absent, the script skips
# pruning and says so, which is the safe direction.
scripts/localization/strings.xcode.json

# Growth & Marketing renders (scripts/growth/build-assets.mjs)
#
# 357 PNGs across 21 languages, ~628 MB — too large to carry in git, and
# unnecessary: the pipeline is deterministic. `npm run growth` re-renders them
# byte-for-byte from the committed art in docs/growth/art/ plus the copy in
# Tidybyte/Resources/Localizable.xcstrings and docs/appstore/listings.json.
#
# The art (4 PNGs), the generator, and the App Store screenshots are all
# committed. Only this derived output is ignored.
docs/growth/*/by-language/

# App Store Connect API private keys (scripts/publish/)
#
# A .p8 signs a JWT that can upload builds, rewrite store copy, and submit for
# review. It is the whole credential, Apple lets you download it exactly once,
# and it cannot be rotated by deleting a file in git history. Keep it out of the
# repo: the publish scripts read it from ASC_KEY_PATH instead.
*.p8
AuthKey_*.p8
